<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01LH">Remark <span data-tag="01LH">4.6.7.9</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a simplicial category containing a pair of objects $X$ and $Y$, and suppose that the simplicial set $\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(X,Y)_{\bullet }$ is an $\infty $-category. Applying Theorem <a data-tag="01LG" href="/tag/01LG">4.6.7.8</a> to the opposite simplicial category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}}$ (and using Remark <a data-tag="01KZ" href="/tag/01KZ">4.6.5.3</a>), we obtain an equivalence of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \theta ': \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(X,Y)_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{op}} \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}^{\mathrm{R}}( X, Y), \]
</div>
<p> which can be described explicitly using a variant of Construction <a data-tag="01LD" href="/tag/01LD">4.6.7.3</a>. </p>
</article>
